{
  "title": "Calorie estimates: lines that reference another recipe or a serving",
  "description": "Lines that name another recipe or an unweighed portion instead of an amount. \"2 portions … (approx. 150 g per person)\" and \"servings\" as a unit already work. \
Left: \"1 recipe guacamole\", \"1 recipe pico de gallo\", \"1/2 recipe the best basic guacamole\", \"1 recipe pizza dough or …\" (Unsupported quantity unit in all three corpora), \"1 batch roasted tomato salsa\", \"1/2 batch Rice Krispies Treats\", \"1 batch Rhubarb Vanilla Compote (recipe below)\"; and 12 \"2 portions cooked Japanese short-grain rice\" plus udon/soba/ramen portions with no weight anywhere on the line. \
A recipe or batch of a sub-recipe can't be weighed; it should probably be reported as not counted with a clearer reason than Unsupported quantity unit (or, longer term, link to the sub-recipe's own estimate). \
Owner decision needed on that half. \
An unweighed portion needs a cited per-portion weight (USDA has none for \"portion\"; Just One Cookbook's own rice guide might state one) or should stay unknown. \
Measure with make ingredient-catalog-audit (Unsupported quantity unit, all three corpora); make pipeline should produce only data/ingredient-catalog-audit.md and fixture-category diffs. \
Server-side only (ramekin-core nutrition), so no web or iOS change. \
Split out of the retired p3-nutrition-remaining-count-units (owner, 2026-10-24: whole groups per PR, never one ingredient).",
